2. THE CLINICAL CONTENT — NOT COVERED BY THE ABOVE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under assets/books/ is clinical reference material, and the
licence above does NOT apply to it. Three separate bodies of work are
bundled there and each carries its own terms.

  assets/books/protocolbook/
      "Quick Reference: Basic Protocols in Paediatrics and Internal
      Medicine for Resource Limited Settings"
      Copyright (c) J. Grey Faulkenberry. All rights reserved.

  assets/books/who_imci/
      "Pocket book of hospital care for children: guidelines for the
      management of common childhood illnesses, 2nd ed."
      (c) World Health Organization 2013. All rights reserved.
      WHO's open access licence applies to material published from
      November 2016; this edition predates it, so reuse requires
      permission from WHO Press. A permissions request was submitted on
      2026-09-02 and, per WHO's terms, confers no authorisation unless
      and until it is approved. See WHO-PERMISSION-REQUEST.md.
      WHO is not responsible for any changes made to the original
      content, and responsibility for this adaptation rests solely with
      the publisher of this application.

  assets/books/wvems/
      "WVEMS Prehospital Protocols, 2026 edition"
      Copyright (c) West Virginia Emergency Medical Services.
      Reproduced as printed. WVEMS is the authority for crews operating
      under these protocols.

  assets/books/wvems/images/
      Representative dosage-form and equipment illustrations from
      Wikimedia Commons, under CC BY, CC BY-SA and CC0. Every author,
      source and licence is listed in assets/credits.yaml and displayed
      in the application on its credits screen, which is what CC BY and
      CC BY-SA require.

Anyone reusing this repository is responsible for obtaining their own
permission for the content in assets/books/. Cloning the code does not
carry any right to redistribute the books.

